.TH DANBY-CHAOSINTRO 1
.SH NAME
danby-chaosintro \- introduction to deterministic chaos
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/chaosintro
.SH DESCRIPTION
Two Lorenz trajectories begin only one millionth of a unit apart.  Their
overlaid phase curves initially coincide, while the lower graph records the
base-10 logarithm of their separation.  A sustained rising interval is direct
evidence of sensitive dependence: deterministic equations can make long-term
prediction impractical without being random.
.PP
Click the lower controls to change sigma, rho, and beta.  Click the phase view
to choose another initial x value.  Space pauses, period advances one step
while paused, and
.B r
resets.
.SH SEE ALSO
danby-chaosdynamics(1), danby-chaos(1), danby-chaosmap(1)
